SU(2) signed-square PSD boundary-reduction stress audit

COMMAND
make -f Makefile.research probe_su2_signed_square_boundary_stress
OMP_NUM_THREADS=26 OMP_DYNAMIC=false \
  ./probe_su2_signed_square_boundary_stress 10000000 24 8

OUTPUT
SU2_SIGNED_SQUARE_BOUNDARY_STRESS samples=10000000 maximum_level=48 maximum_coefficient=8 threads=26 nonnegative_squares=2975212 log_concave_squares=555751 boundary_squares=552952 current_failures=0 insertion_checks=3789146 insertion_failures=0 full_insertion_failures=0 first_failure=(-1,-1,-1,0) first_root=[] first_square=[] first_insertion=(-1,-1,-1,0) first_insertion_root=[] first_insertion_input=[] first_full_insertion=(-1,-1,-1,-1,0) first_full_insertion_root=[] first_full_insertion_input=[] result=NO_PSD_CURRENT_OR_INSERTION_FAILURE

METHOD
The deterministic audit generates 10,000,000 signed integer profiles q
through half-level K=24 using four independent sign-pattern families.
It forms the exact finite fusion square d=q^2.  Because every finite
fusion matrix is real symmetric,

  N_d=N_q^2

is positive semidefinite even though q need not be character-positive.
The audit retains only squares d that are coefficientwise nonnegative,
log concave with interval support, and satisfy every simple-current
boundary.  It then evaluates every anchored current exactly with
signed 64-bit integers.  For every retained profile satisfying the
complete anchored cone, it also applies every nontrivial
irreducible-square transform and checks both the output boundary and
the complete output anchored cone.  The
configured coefficient and level bounds keep every intermediate far
below the signed 64-bit limit.

The thread count is a runtime choice made from contemporaneous CPU load
and available RAM; it is not a mathematical bound or a source-level
limit.  The zero failure counts are bounded evidence for PSD boundary
reduction, PSD boundary insertion, and direct PSD full-cone insertion,
not unbounded proofs.

COMPILER FLAGS
g++ -O2 -std=c++20 -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Wconversion \
  -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror -fopenmp \
  probe_su2_signed_square_boundary_stress.cpp \
  -o probe_su2_signed_square_boundary_stress

